## Answer

Yes — Cargo's `[patch]` table is exactly the mechanism for this, and your instinct about "only ever reference via git" is close but has a problem: it works for consumers, but it can't work for the crate's *own* repo (e.g. `memory-api`'s own `test-cli` can't depend on `test-api` via git pointing at itself — you'd never be able to build against local changes before pushing, and it'd still create two source IDs the moment any other repo's git-fetched code also pulls it in).

**Root cause confirmed via `cargo tree -d`:** duplication wasn't limited to `test-api`/`feedback-api`. The same path-vs-git split affected `ticket`/`ticket-api`, `spec`/`spec-api`, `rule-api`, `doc-http`, `feedback-http`, and even `context-api`/`context-trace`/etc. (pulled in transitively through `viewer-api`, which is itself duplicated the same way).

**Fix applied** in [Cargo.toml](Cargo.toml): extended the existing `memory-kernel` patch pattern to every repo that's both a local submodule (with in-tree path members) and consumed via `git` elsewhere:

```toml
[patch."https://github.com/mankinskin/memory-kernel"]
memory-kernel = { path = "memory-kernel" }
transport-harness = { path = "memory-kernel/crates/transport-harness" }

[patch."https://github.com/mankinskin/context-stack"]
context-api = { path = "context-stack/context-api" }
# ... context-insert, context-read, context-search, context-trace, context-trace-macros, ngrams

[patch."https://github.com/mankinskin/viewer-api"]
viewer-api = { path = "viewer-api" }

[patch."https://github.com/mankinskin/memory-api"]
doc-http = { path = "memory-api/tools/http/doc-http" }
feedback-api = { path = "memory-api/crates/feedback-api" }
feedback-http = { path = "memory-api/tools/http/feedback-http" }
rule-api = { path = "memory-api/crates/rule-api" }
test-api = { path = "memory-api/crates/test-api" }

[patch."https://github.com/mankinskin/ticket"]
ticket = { path = "workflow-tools/ticket" }
ticket-api = { path = "workflow-tools/ticket/crates/ticket-api" }

[patch."https://github.com/mankinskin/spec"]
spec = { path = "workflow-tools/spec" }
spec-api = { path = "workflow-tools/spec/crates/spec-api" }
```

Per the repo's own documented policy, this is dev-workspace composition only — domain manifests keep their canonical `git` declarations, and a "patch-free" build (disable this table, rebuild, check `Cargo.lock` for `git+https://...` sources) is the real acceptance proof before a migration is considered done.

**Verified:** `test-cli` and `rule-cli` (previously failing with `expected test_api::store::TestStoreConfig, found TestStoreConfig`) now build cleanly, and `doc-viewer`/`spec-viewer`/`ticket-viewer` still build.

**Remaining unrelated, pre-existing bug (not touched):** [memory-matrix/src/matrix.rs](memory-api/crates/memory-matrix/src/matrix.rs#L40) and [cli.rs](memory-api/crates/memory-matrix/src/cli.rs) reference nonexistent crates `spec_mcp`/`spec_cli` — these should be `spec::mcp`/`spec::cli` (or `spec_api::cli`) module paths under the new `spec` crate layout. This predates today's changes and is out of scope for the version-duplication fix; let me know if you want it fixed too.

Committed locally as `ec0ee02a` (not pushed, since it's a context-engine-local build config, not a cross-repo API change).

